# Mockito 4.8.0 — Unit Testing Patterns

## 1. Project Setup (JUnit 5 + Mockito)

**Maven dependency:**
```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.mockito</groupId>
    <artifactId>mockito-core</artifactId>
    <version>4.8.0</version>
    <scope>test</scope>
</dependency>
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.mockito</groupId>
    <artifactId>mockito-junit-jupiter</artifactId>
    <version>4.8.0</version>
    <scope>test</scope>
</dependency>
```

---

## 2. `@ExtendWith` + `@MockitoExtension` — Core Test Structure

This is the **preferred JUnit 5 approach** — no Spring context, pure unit test speed.

```java
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.BeforeEach;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.extension.ExtendWith;
import org.mockito.Mock;
import org.mockito.InjectMocks;
import org.mockito.junit.jupiter.MockitoExtension;

@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)
class LeadServiceTest {

    @Mock
    private LeadRepository leadRepository;       // dependency — auto-created mock

    @Mock
    private NotificationService notificationService;

    @InjectMocks
    private LeadService leadService;             // system under test — mocks injected automatically

    @BeforeEach
    void setUp(@Mock AuditService auditService) {
        // @Mock can also be injected into @BeforeEach and @Test method parameters
    }

    @Test
    void shouldReturnLeadById() {
        // ...
    }
}
```

**Key rules:**
- `@Mock` — creates a mock of the type; all methods return default values (`null`, `0`, `false`) unless stubbed.
- `@InjectMocks` — instantiates the class under test and injects all `@Mock` fields (by constructor, setter, or field injection — in that priority order).
- `@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)` — activates annotation processing; replaces the old `MockitoAnnotations.openMocks(this)` in `@BeforeEach`.
- `@Spy` — wraps a real object; real methods are called unless explicitly stubbed.
- `@Captor` — shorthand for declaring an `ArgumentCaptor` field.

---

## 3. Stubbing with `when().thenReturn()`

Always stub **before** the act step (Arrange → Act → Assert).

```java
@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)
class LeadServiceTest {

    @Mock
    private LeadRepository leadRepository;

    @InjectMocks
    private LeadService leadService;

    @Test
    void shouldFindLeadById() {
        // Arrange — define mock behavior
        Lead mockLead = new Lead("L001", "Solar", "OPEN");
        when(leadRepository.findById("L001")).thenReturn(Optional.of(mockLead));

        // Act
        Lead result = leadService.getLeadById("L001");

        // Assert
        assertThat(result.getId()).isEqualTo("L001");
        assertThat(result.getStatus()).isEqualTo("OPEN");
    }

    @Test
    void shouldReturnEmptyWhenLeadNotFound() {
        when(leadRepository.findById("UNKNOWN")).thenReturn(Optional.empty());

        assertThatThrownBy(() -> leadService.getLeadById("UNKNOWN"))
            .isInstanceOf(LeadNotFoundException.class);
    }

    @Test
    void shouldThrowWhenRepositoryFails() {
        // Stub to throw an exception
        when(leadRepository.findById(anyString()))
            .thenThrow(new RuntimeException("DB connection failed"));

        assertThatThrownBy(() -> leadService.getLeadById("L001"))
            .isInstanceOf(RuntimeException.class)
            .hasMessage("DB connection failed");
    }
}
```

**Common stubbing variants:**
```java
when(mock.method()).thenReturn(value);          // return a value
when(mock.method()).thenThrow(new Ex());        // throw exception
when(mock.method()).thenReturn(v1).thenReturn(v2); // return different values on consecutive calls
doThrow(new Ex()).when(mock).voidMethod();      // for void methods
doNothing().when(mock).voidMethod();           // explicit no-op for void
```

---

## 4. Verifying Interactions with `verify()`

```java
@Test
void shouldSaveLeadAndSendNotification() {
    // Arrange
    Lead lead = new Lead("L002", "Solar", "NEW");
    when(leadRepository.save(any(Lead.class))).thenReturn(lead);

    // Act
    leadService.createLead(lead);

    // Assert interactions
    verify(leadRepository).save(lead);                         // called exactly once (default)
    verify(notificationService).sendEmail(anyString());        // called with any string
    verify(leadRepository, times(1)).save(any(Lead.class));   // explicit times
    verify(leadRepository, never()).delete(any());             // never called
    verify(notificationService, atLeastOnce()).sendEmail(anyString());
    verify(notificationService, atMost(2)).sendEmail(anyString());
}

@Test
void shouldVerifyNoMoreInteractionsAfterSave() {
    leadService.createLead(new Lead("L003", "Wind", "NEW"));

    verify(leadRepository).save(any());
    verifyNoMoreInteractions(leadRepository);   // no other methods were called on this mock
    verifyNoInteractions(auditService);         // this mock was never touched at all
}
```

