## 3. `@DataMongoTest` — Repository Layer Testing

`@DataMongoTest` configures an embedded MongoDB (via `de.flapdoodle.embed.mongo`), scans for `@Document` classes, and wires up Spring Data MongoDB repositories.

```java
import org.junit.jupiter.api.AfterEach;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.boot.test.autoconfigure.data.mongo.DataMongoTest;
import org.springframework.data.mongodb.core.MongoTemplate;

import static org.assertj.core.api.Assertions.assertThat;

@DataMongoTest
class LeadRepositoryTest {

    @Autowired
    private LeadRepository leadRepository;      // real repository, wired to embedded Mongo

    @Autowired
    private MongoTemplate mongoTemplate;        // for setup/teardown operations

    @AfterEach
    void cleanUp() {
        leadRepository.deleteAll();             // isolate each test
    }

    @Test
    void shouldSaveAndFindLead() {
        Lead lead = new Lead(null, "Solar Install", "OPEN");
        Lead saved = leadRepository.save(lead);

        assertThat(saved.getId()).isNotNull();

        Lead found = leadRepository.findById(saved.getId()).orElseThrow();
        assertThat(found.getTitle()).isEqualTo("Solar Install");
        assertThat(found.getStatus()).isEqualTo("OPEN");
    }

    @Test
    void shouldFindLeadsByStatus() {
        leadRepository.saveAll(List.of(
            new Lead(null, "Lead A", "OPEN"),
            new Lead(null, "Lead B", "CLOSED"),
            new Lead(null, "Lead C", "OPEN")
        ));

        List<Lead> openLeads = leadRepository.findByStatus("OPEN");

        assertThat(openLeads).hasSize(2)
            .extracting(Lead::getTitle)
            .containsExactlyInAnyOrder("Lead A", "Lead C");
    }

    @Test
    void shouldUseMongoTemplateForComplexSetup() {
        mongoTemplate.save(new Lead(null, "Template Lead", "PENDING"), "leads");

        long count = mongoTemplate.count(new Query(), Lead.class);
        assertThat(count).isEqualTo(1);
    }
}
```

**Against a real MongoDB (skip embedded):**
```java
@DataMongoTest(excludeAutoConfiguration = EmbeddedMongoAutoConfiguration.class)
class LeadRepositoryRealMongoTest {
    // connects to MongoDB defined in application-test.properties
}
```

