## 4. Service Layer — Pure Mockito (No Spring Context)

Service tests are the most common and should **never** load a Spring context. Pure `@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)` is the right tool.

```java
@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)
class LeadWorkflowServiceTest {

    @Mock
    private LeadRepository leadRepository;

    @Mock
    private WorkflowEngine workflowEngine;

    @Mock
    private AuditService auditService;

    @InjectMocks
    private LeadWorkflowService leadWorkflowService;  // the service being tested

    @Captor
    private ArgumentCaptor<WorkflowEvent> eventCaptor;

    @Test
    void shouldTransitionLeadToInProgress() {
        // Arrange
        Lead lead = new Lead("L001", "Solar", "OPEN");
        when(leadRepository.findById("L001")).thenReturn(Optional.of(lead));
        when(leadRepository.save(any(Lead.class))).thenAnswer(inv -> inv.getArgument(0));

        // Act
        leadWorkflowService.startWork("L001");

        // Assert — state change
        verify(leadRepository).save(leadCaptor.capture());  // wait — use the @Captor
        // use eventCaptor for the WorkflowEngine
        verify(workflowEngine).publish(eventCaptor.capture());

        WorkflowEvent event = eventCaptor.getValue();
        assertThat(event.getLeadId()).isEqualTo("L001");
        assertThat(event.getTransition()).isEqualTo("OPEN -> IN_PROGRESS");

        // Assert — side effects
        verify(auditService, times(1)).log(eq("L001"), anyString());
    }

    @Test
    void shouldNotTransitionIfLeadAlreadyClosed() {
        Lead closedLead = new Lead("L002", "Solar", "CLOSED");
        when(leadRepository.findById("L002")).thenReturn(Optional.of(closedLead));

        assertThatThrownBy(() -> leadWorkflowService.startWork("L002"))
            .isInstanceOf(InvalidLeadStateException.class)
            .hasMessageContaining("CLOSED");

        verify(leadRepository, never()).save(any());
        verifyNoInteractions(workflowEngine);
        verifyNoInteractions(auditService);
    }
}
```

