## 5. `@MockBean` vs `@Mock` — Critical Distinction

| | `@Mock` (Mockito) | `@MockBean` (Spring Boot Test) |
|---|---|---|
| **Context** | No Spring context needed | Requires a Spring context (`@WebMvcTest`, `@SpringBootTest`) |
| **Used with** | `@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)` | `@WebMvcTest`, `@DataMongoTest`, `@SpringBootTest` |
| **Registered as** | Local field in the test class | A Spring Bean in the application context |
| **Resets between tests** | Yes (new mock per test) | Yes (reset after each test by default) |
| **Purpose** | Service / unit layer testing | Replace a Spring-managed dependency in a slice |

