## 6. Best Practices for Test Organization

### Package structure (mirror production)
```
src/
  main/java/com/company/integration/
    controller/LeadController.java
    service/LeadService.java
    repository/LeadRepository.java
  test/java/com/company/integration/
    controller/LeadControllerTest.java     <- @WebMvcTest
    service/LeadServiceTest.java           <- @ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)
    repository/LeadRepositoryTest.java     <- @DataMongoTest
    integration/LeadIntegrationTest.java   <- @SpringBootTest (sparingly)
```

### Naming conventions
```java
// Method name pattern: should[ExpectedBehavior]When[StateUnderTest]
void shouldReturnLeadWhenIdIsValid()
void shouldThrowNotFoundWhenLeadDoesNotExist()
void shouldSendEmailWhenLeadIsCreated()
void shouldNotSaveWhenValidationFails()
```

### AAA structure (Arrange / Act / Assert) — always use comments
```java
@Test
void shouldCloseLeadAndNotifyAssignee() {
    // Arrange
    Lead lead = new Lead("L001", "Solar", "OPEN");
    when(leadRepository.findById("L001")).thenReturn(Optional.of(lead));

    // Act
    leadService.closeLead("L001", "Completed successfully");

    // Assert
    verify(leadRepository).save(any());
    verify(notificationService).sendEmail(eq("assignee@company.com"), anyString());
}
```

### Additional best practices
- **One logical assertion per test** — keep tests focused; use multiple `verify()` and `assertThat()` only when they test the same behavior.
- **Never use `@SpringBootTest` for unit or service layer tests** — it loads the full context and is 10-100x slower.
- **Use `verifyNoMoreInteractions()` sparingly** — it makes tests brittle; prefer explicit `verify()` calls for what matters.
- **Prefer constructor injection** in production code — `@InjectMocks` works most reliably with constructor injection, and it makes dependencies explicit.
- **Do not stub what you don't use** — `MockitoExtension` in strict mode (default in 4.x) will fail the test if there are unused stubs, catching dead test code early.
- **Isolate `@DataMongoTest` tests** — always `deleteAll()` in `@AfterEach` to prevent test pollution between methods.
- **Use `@WebMvcTest(SpecificController.class)`** — always name the controller to avoid loading all controllers in the package.

